# What must never enter the build context.
#
# The first two entries are the ones that matter. `.env` holds real credentials and `COPY . .` would
# put it in a layer — where it stays, readable, even if a later step deletes it. `data/` is somebody's
# database and log.
#
# The rest is speed: `node_modules` is reinstalled in the image anyway, and sending a few hundred
# megabytes of it to the daemon on every build is time spent for nothing.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
data
*.log

node_modules
.svelte-kit
build
test-results
playwright-report

.git
.github
.husky
.vscode
.references

README.md
